# Fixed 2026-10-01 by lane 135c (defect 141, a shape beside it). Symptom:
# this file's last byte is a carriage return with no line feed after it,
# which the lexer refuses anywhere else as `stray_carriage_return`; on the
# compiler of `9d1c209d`, `check` passed it at exit 0 while `fmt`, which
# reads the file alone, refused it. Cause: `source.from_files` closed the
# open last line with a newline of its own, so the lexer read `\r\n`, a line
# ending its author never wrote. A file is now read in a compilation byte
# for byte as it is read alone. No `certain` fix: `--apply` owes it back
# as it is.

function main()
    #~v stray_carriage_return
    print(1)